<title>SOUTH AFRICA: U.S. Colgate buys stake in S.African firm.</title>
<headline>U.S. Colgate buys stake in S.African firm.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. home products giant Colgate-Palmolive Ltd has bought an unspecified stake in private South African hair care group Black Like Me, the firm said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Black Like Me, with annual sales of more than 50 million rand, markets a range of black hair care products. The firm was founded in 1985 by local entrepreneur Herman Mashaba.</p>
<p>Mashaba will retain an equity interest in the firm and remain as chairman and managing director.</p>
<p>The firm said the alliance with Colgate-Palmolive would allow it to expand internationally.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
